WEBVTT

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.932
Something changed while you slept.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:11.343
You do what you always do. Read the
filing, re-type the numbers, check the

00:00:11.343 --> 00:00:12.434
reason still holds.

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:19.661
One page. Five things. Ranked by how much
of your money depends on them.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.729
This one reported overnight.

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.328
Every fact we extract points back at the
sentence it came from.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:32.846
Your model updates, as a proposal, with
the source attached. You approve it.

00:00:33.126 --> 00:00:38.767
Then the part nobody else does. The reason
you own it is assumptions with thresholds.

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:39.895
One just broke.

00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:44.650
Five positions depend on it. Two you would
never have connected yourself.

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:48.878
Whatever you decide is recorded with
everything that was known when you decided

00:00:48.878 --> 00:00:49.182
it.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.858
Terminals tell you what happened.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.419
Quantify Terminal tells you what changed
because it happened.
